```

Wait — but the plan says "Do NOT add code comments unless the plan explicitly requires them." Hmm, that's from AGENTS.md under "Adding a New Rule" — but this is a mechanical refactor task, and the established repo pattern for check files includes `//!` module docs. The plan's own layout shows "check_*.rs  # one file per independent check". I think a one-line `//!` doc per check file is appropriate and matches the repo's established convention (performance/formatting check files all have them). It's not really a "code comment" — it's module documentation. I'll add minimal one-liners.

